WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.468
Job two: take care of your people.

2
00:00:03.518 --> 00:00:10.183
Why it matters: people stay, and do their best work, for a manager who notices them.

3
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:14.419
This is where your team’s engagement is made or lost.

4
00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:15.379
Four habits.

5
00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:24.092
Listen and help: someone mentions a hard week at home; you listen, move what you can, and check in on Monday.

6
00:00:24.142 --> 00:00:30.327
And know the line: if they mention leave, a health issue, or unfair treatment,

7
00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:36.083
send it to the right office the same day, and never ask for a diagnosis.

8
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:43.677
Grow them: once a quarter, without a form, ask what each person wants to be doing in two years,

9
00:00:43.727 --> 00:00:47.594
and find one assignment that stretches toward it.

10
00:00:47.644 --> 00:00:55.268
Thank them: the way you handled the vendor call on Thursday kept us on schedule, said on Friday.

11
00:00:55.318 --> 00:01:00.304
Specific, by name, that week. Great job everyone thanks nobody.

12
00:01:00.354 --> 00:01:08.378
Trust them: hand over the decision, not just the task, and ask the team before you set a new process.

13
00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:15.972
What to stop doing: being friendly instead of helpful, and saving growth for the annual review.

14
00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:20.049
This week: thank one person for one specific thing.

15
00:01:20.099 --> 00:01:23.166
Now flip the cards, then turn the page.

